{"authored" [{"question" "q-352246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "8087c502fa2791d10cb516f3278569f14271cfbc0bf17fcb44d7ea90ba1dc15f" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $1$ | $8$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-4$ | $-16$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $-9$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}=x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{3}+4x\\,{|}_{0}^{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})+4(3-0)-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+4|) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}+12-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{2}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{4}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "8087c502fa2791d10cb516f3278569f14271cfbc0bf17fcb44d7ea90ba1dc15f" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "8087c502fa2791d10cb516f3278569f14271cfbc0bf17fcb44d7ea90ba1dc15f" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "8087c502fa2791d10cb516f3278569f14271cfbc0bf17fcb44d7ea90ba1dc15f" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "8087c502fa2791d10cb516f3278569f14271cfbc0bf17fcb44d7ea90ba1dc15f" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $4$ | $-5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $\\frac{8}{3}$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-\\frac{7}{3}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)} & =4-\\frac{(7/3)}{(x-2/3)} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{7}{3x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(4-\\frac{7}{3x-2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x-7{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[4x-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4(3-1)-\\frac{7}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[8-\\frac{7\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "8087c502fa2791d10cb516f3278569f14271cfbc0bf17fcb44d7ea90ba1dc15f" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ceddb81d44941092b2f1e7cce986711c1f96bf17c9acae17f5d36a72695a804" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "8087c502fa2791d10cb516f3278569f14271cfbc0bf17fcb44d7ea90ba1dc15f" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/state.json" "file_sha256" "8087c502fa2791d10cb516f3278569f14271cfbc0bf17fcb44d7ea90ba1dc15f" "basis" 1751 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14051235/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-114894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-114894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3(x-\\frac{1}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{(x-\\frac{1}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 2 & 5 \\\\  & ↓ & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{17}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+5}{(x-\\frac{1}{3})} & =2+\\frac{(\\frac{17}{3})}{(x-\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{17}{3(x-\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{17}{3x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{2x+5}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(2+\\frac{17}{3x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\text{d}x+17{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[2x+\\frac{17}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-1|]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(0-(-1))+\\frac{17}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3(0)-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3(-1)-1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(1)+\\frac{17}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2-\\frac{17}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2-\\frac{34}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}[3-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-114894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ccbde14e50f31661d6ec646abc5189f1edf2151512484371e06ed936ba22644"} {"question" "q-114894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-114894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{9}[3-11\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}[1-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}[3-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}[17-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}[4-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-114894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{9}[3-17\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+3}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $5$ | $3$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+3}{x+1}=x+4-\\frac{1}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+3}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(x+4-\\frac{1}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4}+4x\\,{|}_{1}^{4}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({4}^{2}-{1}^{2})+4(4-1)-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+1|) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}+12-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{5}{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352241" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ccbde14e50f31661d6ec646abc5189f1edf2151512484371e06ed936ba22644"} {"question" "q-352241" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352241" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{39}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352241" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352241" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $1$ | $8$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-4$ | $-16$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $-9$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}=x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{3}+4x\\,{|}_{0}^{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})+4(3-0)-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+4|) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}+12-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{2}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{4}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ccbde14e50f31661d6ec646abc5189f1edf2151512484371e06ed936ba22644"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{33}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352246" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-7}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{43}{25}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $5$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-7}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-7}{5(x+\\frac{1}{5})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-7}{(x+\\frac{1}{5})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{5}$ | $8$ | $-7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{8}{5}$ |\n|  | $8$ | $-\\frac{43}{5}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-7}{(x+\\frac{1}{5})} & =8-\\frac{(\\frac{43}{5})}{(x+\\frac{1}{5})} \\\\  & =8-\\frac{43}{5x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8x-7}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(8-\\frac{43}{5x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[8{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-43{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{[8x-\\frac{43}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|5x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[8(1-0)-\\frac{43}{5}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{43}{25}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ccbde14e50f31661d6ec646abc5189f1edf2151512484371e06ed936ba22644"} {"question" "q-352426" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352426" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352426" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-352426" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $4$ | $-5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $\\frac{8}{3}$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-\\frac{7}{3}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)} & =4-\\frac{(7/3)}{(x-2/3)} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{7}{3x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(4-\\frac{7}{3x-2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x-7{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[4x-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4(3-1)-\\frac{7}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[8-\\frac{7\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f130894b8f1f91dcc3802f4e17319b258b7894dda71680fb94eaf6b6ba1c3b3"} {"question" "q-358987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053187/activity-metadata.json" "